---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '16 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Vaelor Trading LLC handles member data.">
  <main class="shell scroll-reveal">
    <article class="prose" style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 0 72px">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-dim)">Last updated {updated}.</p>
      <div class="mono" style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-faint)">
        Legal · Members
      </div>

      <p>
        This policy explains what Vaelor Trading LLC ("Vaelor", "we") collects when you create a member
        account or use the member dashboard, why we collect it, and the choices you have. It applies to
        <code>vaelor.pages.dev</code> and the member dashboard at <code>/member</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Data</th><th>When</th><th>Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Email address, display name, optional first/last name</td>
            <td>Registration, or your first Google/GitHub sign-in</td>
            <td>Identify your account, contact you about it</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Password hash (PBKDF2-SHA256, 100 000 iterations, per-user salt)</td>
            <td>When you choose email + password sign-in</td>
            <td>Sign you in. We never store your password itself.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>OAuth account identifier from Google or GitHub</td>
            <td>Only if you use that provider</td>
            <td>Link the provider to your existing account so you can sign in either way</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Session token</td>
            <td>Every sign-in</td>
            <td>Keep you signed in. Stored server-side as a hash, in your browser as an HttpOnly cookie.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Plan, subscription status and expiry</td>
            <td>When the desk activates or changes a plan</td>
            <td>Decide which features your account can open</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Sign-in timestamps, IP address, failed-attempt counters</td>
            <td>Every authentication attempt</td>
            <td>Rate limiting, abuse prevention, and the owner's security console</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Bridge endpoint and pairing token</td>
            <td>When you pair a MetaTrader 5 bridge instance</td>
            <td>Talk to your own cloud bridge. The token is kept in your browser, not in our database.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To run the service you asked for: sign you in, keep your session, and show the tools your plan includes.</li>
        <li>To secure the service: rate limiting, detecting credential stuffing, and an audit trail of account actions.</li>
        <li>To answer you when you contact the desk, and to tell you about your subscription.</li>
        <li>To meet legal obligations and enforce this policy.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell member data, and we do not use your account data for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Item</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>vaelor_session</code></td>
            <td>First-party cookie, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure on HTTPS</td>
            <td>Server-side session</td>
            <td>30 days, or 180 days with "Remember me"</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>localStorage</code> keys such as <code>vaelor_profile_v1</code>, <code>vaelor_bridge_v1</code></td>
            <td>Browser storage</td>
            <td>Remember your dashboard preferences and your own bridge endpoint and token</td>
            <td>Until you clear it or unpair</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        The dashboard reads your session from the server on every page load. The browser copy is a cache,
        so an outage cannot sign you in or keep you signed in on its own.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <b>Hosting and storage:</b> Cloudflare (Pages hosting and KV storage of account records).
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Sign-in providers:</b> Google or GitHub, but only if you choose them. They receive the
          information needed to complete that sign-in and nothing else.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Your broker:</b> MetaTrader 5 bridge traffic goes between your browser and your own bridge
          instance. Vaelor does not hold your broker credentials.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Payment processing:</b> if a payment processor is enabled, it receives the billing details
          needed to take payment. Card numbers never reach us.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep your account record while your account exists. Sessions expire on the schedule above.
        Failed-login counters expire within 15 minutes. Audit entries are kept for 180 days.
        If you close your account, we delete the account record and its subscription record within 30 days,
        except where we must keep a record to meet a legal obligation.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Security</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Passwords are hashed with PBKDF2-SHA256 and a random per-user salt. Plaintext passwords are never stored or logged.</li>
        <li>Session tokens are random, opaque, and stored server-side as a hash; the cookie is HttpOnly and Secure on HTTPS.</li>
        <li>Plan changes are written only by owner-authenticated endpoints. A member cannot grant themselves a plan.</li>
        <li>OAuth logins verify the provider's signed identity and require a verified email before an account is created.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You can sign in with a password, Google, or GitHub, and add a second method later.</li>
        <li>You can unpair your bridge at any time from the account panel, which removes the token from this browser.</li>
        <li>You can ask for a copy or deletion of your account data by emailing the address below.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>The service is for adults 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, we will update the date above and, where the change affects
        how we use your data, tell members through the dashboard or by email.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or requests about your data: <a href="mailto:mahdi.t8256@gmail.com">mahdi.t8256@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:28px"><a href="/terms">Terms of Service →</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>